From d341a0c2d970ab1a03ceb7d58e32cbbfe35448ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:04:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] uhf: fix the CRC16 polynomial to match the platform's
 corrected value

Companion to frameworks/base's fix confirming the real polynomial is
0x8408 (proven back to back on real hardware against the previous
CRC-16/MODBUS guess, poly 0xA001 - see that commit for the full byte-
level proof). This header is a deliberate, line-for-line-equivalent port
of com.android.server.uhf.UhfProtocol's CRC16 logic, and per its own
header comment, when the two ever diverge the Java version is the source
of truth to re-port from, not to fix independently - done exactly that
way here.

Still not independently build-tested in C++ in this pass (no build of
this HAL has been attempted from this environment), same as every other
change to this file - its correctness rests on being a faithful port of
the now-hardware-confirmed Java algorithm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 aidl/default/UhfWireProtocol.h | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/aidl/default/UhfWireProtocol.h b/aidl/default/UhfWireProtocol.h
index 762733f..a36f1a8 100644
--- a/aidl/default/UhfWireProtocol.h
+++ b/aidl/default/UhfWireProtocol.h
@@ -40,8 +40,14 @@ namespace uhf {
 constexpr int kMinLenField = 4;
 constexpr int kMaxLenField = 0xFF;
 constexpr int kAddressBroadcast = 0xFF;
-constexpr uint16_t kCrc16Init = 0xFFFF; // CRC-16/MODBUS; see UhfProtocol.java's doc on this being
-                                         // an inference pending R1, isolated to one constant.
+// Confirmed on real hardware, not an inference: poly 0x8408 (reflected form of 0x1021), init
+// 0xFFFF, no xorout. The MODBUS guess (poly 0xA001) was wrong - proven back to back on the wire
+// with a real reader, HAL stopped: frame 04 ff 21 with the MODBUS CRC (b1 e9) was silently
+// ignored; the same frame with this CRC (19 95) got a full reply. See UhfProtocol.java's doc for
+// the exact byte-level proof. Only this one constant differs from the MODBUS algorithm - same
+// init, same reflected/LSB-first structure - which is exactly why this was ever isolated to one
+// constant in the first place.
+constexpr uint16_t kCrc16Init = 0xFFFF;
 
 inline uint16_t crc16(const uint8_t* data, size_t length) {
     uint32_t crc = kCrc16Init;
@@ -51,7 +57,7 @@ inline uint16_t crc16(const uint8_t* data, size_t length) {
             bool lsbSet = (crc & 0x0001) != 0;
             crc >>= 1;
             if (lsbSet) {
-                crc ^= 0xA001;
+                crc ^= 0x8408;
             }
         }
     }
